<p class="brand-line">{{ site.name }} covers artificial intelligence and links the source for each story.</p>
<p>{{ site.name }} is a news desk. It covers artificial intelligence across five sections: Models &amp; Research, Industry &amp; Business, Policy &amp; Regulation, Tools &amp; Products, and Funding.</p>
<p>Each story says what a primary source reported, links that source, and stops where the source stops. The desk does not invent quotes, numbers, or customer claims. The standard is written down in the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>
<p>The site is static. Pages are built from Markdown files in this repository and published on GitHub Pages. There is no account system. Each page loads a Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon, described in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
<h2>How to read a story</h2>
<p>The standfirst under the headline is a summary. The body is the reporting. The source list at the bottom is the set of documents the story relies on. The byline shows when the story was last updated. A factual fix is labeled as a correction. Sourcing and ethics rules are on the <a href="/editorial-policy/">sources and ethics</a> page.</p>
